(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["From Qubits to Fock Space with Wolfram Quantum Framework", "Title",
 CellID->1838735994,ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell["Mads Bahrami \[Bullet] 2026", "Author",
 CellID->1722222643,ExpressionUUID->"4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],

Cell["\<\
Wolfram Quantum Framework treats states, operators, channels, measurements, \
and circuits as symbolic objects that compose. This webinar follows one idea \
across several physical settings: parameters should survive the computation. \
We begin with a symbolic qubit, derive an exact QAOA landscape, and watch a \
Heisenberg interaction generate entanglement. The same object model then \
describes amplitude damping, a generalized measurement, and a spin-1 basis \
transformation. We finish in bosonic Fock space with coherent and cat states, \
then expose the tensor network behind a circuit. The goal is not a catalog of \
functions, but a compact demonstration of one algebra spanning distinct \
quantum problems.\
\>", "Abstract",
 CellID->-1358391428,ExpressionUUID->"1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],

Cell["\<\
Quantum software often separates qubit circuits, open systems, spin models, \
and quantum optics into different computational worlds. Wolfram Quantum \
Framework takes the opposite view: these are different objects in one algebra.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1157928379,ExpressionUUID->"75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],

Cell["\<\
The decisive feature is not merely that symbols are accepted as input. \
Symbols survive composition. A parameter introduced in a state, gate, \
channel, or Hamiltonian can propagate through an entire workflow and return \
as an exact physical statement.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2145511919,ExpressionUUID->"25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The examples target Wolfram Quantum Framework 2.1.0 and Wolfram Language \
14.3 or later. Participants should install the ",
 ButtonBox["paclet",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://resources.wolframcloud.com/PacletRepository/resources/\
Wolfram/QuantumFramework/"], None}],
 " before the session."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1967435313,ExpressionUUID->"00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],

Cell["Load the framework and its continuous-variable extension:", "CodeText",
 CellID->1806749867,ExpressionUUID->"2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`\>\"", "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`SecondQuantization`\>\"",
   "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",
 CellID->749839597,ExpressionUUID->"5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],

Cell["A state can represent a whole family", "Section",
 CellID->-1416150482,ExpressionUUID->"56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Begin with the general pure qubit ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "Ket"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["cos",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], 
     TemplateBox[{"0"},
      "Ket"]}], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
      StyleBox[
       RowBox[{"i", "\[Beta]"}], "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["sin",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], 
     TemplateBox[{"1"},
      "Ket"]}]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],
 ". The state is stored once, with both parameters intact."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2011952198,ExpressionUUID->"3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],

Cell["Construct the symbolic state:", "CodeText",
 CellID->-1393152451,ExpressionUUID->"166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"psi", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "\[Alpha]", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{"I", " ", "\[Beta]"}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "\[Alpha]", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",
 CellID->-987103888,ExpressionUUID->"234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],

Cell["\<\
Its Bloch vector is an exact map from amplitudes to geometry:\
\>", "CodeText",
 CellID->705697581,ExpressionUUID->"6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{"ComplexExpand", "[", 
   RowBox[{"psi", "[", "\"\<BlochVector\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",
 CellID->-367287258,ExpressionUUID->"0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The result is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["\[Beta]", "TI"]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["\[Beta]", "TI"]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox[")",
     FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],
 ". One object represents every pure qubit and exposes its physical geometry \
without numerical sampling."
}], "Text",
 CellID->-1301240748,ExpressionUUID->"23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"],

Cell["A circuit can become an exact landscape", "Section",
 CellID->-296820613,ExpressionUUID->"6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same symbolic propagation reaches through a variational circuit. For \
MaxCut on the complete graph ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["K", "TI"], "4"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"],
 ", one QAOA layer has two angles, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"],
 " for the cost layer and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"],
 " for the mixer."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1951376143,ExpressionUUID->"2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"],

Cell["\<\
Define the graph and derive its dimensions from the graph itself:\
\>", "CodeText",
 CellID->1643770968,ExpressionUUID->"76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"graph", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"CompleteGraph", "[", "4", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"n", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"VertexCount", "[", "graph", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"edges", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"List", " ", "@@@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"EdgeList", "[", "graph", "]"}]}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",
 CellID->-1046987702,ExpressionUUID->"0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Build ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["C", "TI"]], "=", 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["j", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1], "\[Element]", 
     StyleBox["E", "TI"]}],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"],
 " directly from those edges:"
}], "CodeText",
 CellID->1364465120,ExpressionUUID->"741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"hCost", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"id", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
           RowBox[{"StringRepeat", "[", 
            RowBox[{"\"\<I\>\"", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], "]"}], "/", "2"}]}], 
        "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"id", " ", "-", " ", 
           RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"\"\<ZZ\>\"", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}]}], " ", 
          "&"}], ")"}], " ", "/@", " ", "edges"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Label\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Hamiltonian\>\""}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",
 CellID->-1671326553,ExpressionUUID->"3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Prepare ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   TemplateBox[{"+"},
    "Ket"], 
   RowBox[{"\[CircleTimes]", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],
 ":"
}], "CodeText",
 CellID->2013444789,ExpressionUUID->"3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"prep", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"StringRepeat", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<0\>\"", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<H\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Range", "[", "n", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Label\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Prep\>\""}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",
 CellID->-168614079,ExpressionUUID->"1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"],

Cell["Make one cost rotation for every graph edge:", "CodeText",
 CellID->-1372250173,ExpressionUUID->"77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"cost", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\"\<R\>\"", "[", 
         RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", ",", " ", "\"\<ZZ\>\""}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
        "#"}], " ", "&"}], ")"}], " ", "/@", " ", "edges"}], ",", "\n", 
    "    ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Parameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "\[Gamma]", "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Label\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Cost\>\""}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",
 CellID->209018337,ExpressionUUID->"04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"],

Cell["Make the transverse-field mixer:", "CodeText",
 CellID->128329290,ExpressionUUID->"1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"mixer", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<RX\>\"", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Range", "[", "n", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Parameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "\[Theta]", "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Label\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Mixer\>\""}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",
 CellID->2144417420,ExpressionUUID->"6ecb37d0-fbcc-3e82-16c8-ae9dfe7e84e8"],

Cell["Compose the ansatz without reducing any block to a matrix:", "CodeText",
 CellID->1887346208,ExpressionUUID->"4c358d3e-86d3-ec5f-75ca-25783367b6a5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"oneLayer", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"prep", ",", " ", "cost", ",", " ", "mixer"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
    "    ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Parameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\[Theta]", ",", " ", "\[Gamma]"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[9]:= ",
 CellID->-111206173,ExpressionUUID->"1f908cf3-3c70-d55a-45af-25bdb50abfa0"],

Cell["\<\
The expectation value is itself a composable bra-operator-ket circuit:\
\>", "CodeText",
 CellID->697723727,ExpressionUUID->"5dac66ba-272d-3627-0b54-7fe452d99d0d"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"meanValue", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"oneLayer", " ", "/*", " ", "hCost", " ", "/*", " ", 
    RowBox[{"oneLayer", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"meanValue", "[", "\"\<Diagram\>\"", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[10]:= ",
 CellID->297843492,ExpressionUUID->"110914de-bbdd-83a1-4736-8d983e69d18b"],

Cell["\<\
Evaluating that object returns the entire variational objective as one \
formula:\
\>", "CodeText",
 CellID->-494365886,ExpressionUUID->"76d004f9-29e5-6665-1eef-9da34f904d4f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"landscape", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"meanValue", "[", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Scalar\>\"", "]"}], ",", "\n",
     "    ", 
    RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", ",", " ", "\[Theta]"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "Reals"}],
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[11]:= ",
 CellID->287537182,ExpressionUUID->"2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"],

Cell["The result is", "Text",
 CellID->1142172250,ExpressionUUID->"35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["C", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    FractionBox["3", "8"], "(", 
    RowBox[{"7", "+", 
     StyleBox["cos",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "2", 
     StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "+", "2", 
     StyleBox["cos",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "4", 
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["sin",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "-", "8", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["cos",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["sin",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["sin",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "2", 
     StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}], ")"}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->-826862778,ExpressionUUID->"4ebf3687-f906-130d-7644-afe0f8b37e57"],

Cell["\<\
An experiment estimates points on this surface. Here the surface is the \
result.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->-1518177805,ExpressionUUID->"65de4a87-3471-cd9f-13e6-63e1bd0597e5"],

Cell["Plot the exact objective before optimizing it:", "CodeText",
 CellID->1360184697,ExpressionUUID->"7bedd9bd-1d84-ddaa-2992-d0e79436a7f0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Plot3D", "[", 
  RowBox[{"landscape", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "Pi"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\[Theta]", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "Pi"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AxesLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<\[Gamma]\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<\[Theta]\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<cost\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{"ColorFunction", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<TemperatureMap\>\""}], ",", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotPoints", " ", "->", " ", "50"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[12]:= ",
 CellID->-1597398595,ExpressionUUID->"4c37f35a-e1a6-07fe-75cc-eb0790536dc4"],

Cell["\<\
Because the objective remains symbolic, its optimum can be certified \
algebraically rather than read from a grid:\
\>", "CodeText",
 CellID->144555990,ExpressionUUID->"02f88238-86c8-66df-3287-2462337d4c25"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Maximize", "[", 
  RowBox[{"landscape", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\[Theta]", ",", " ", "\[Gamma]"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[13]:= ",
 CellID->2018877569,ExpressionUUID->"034d641c-5834-e412-3173-7e4659c6cf78"],

Cell["\<\
The maximum and the optimizing angles are exact algebraic numbers. This is \
the useful meaning of symbolic variational computation: not symbolic gates in \
isolation, but an analytic objective at the end of the circuit.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->334058132,ExpressionUUID->"52ce4f6a-032d-a48b-02f6-6734b6d90ed1"],

Cell["Evolution can produce a formula for entanglement", "Section",
 CellID->-692712678,ExpressionUUID->"5bfe104a-50de-a555-0985-8a1461680fbf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now replace the circuit by a many-body Hamiltonian. Let two spins interact \
through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["J", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "134534fb-1061-d656-417a-ada5a115bcbc"],
 ", beginning in the product state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"01"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2cd98fd2-34e7-e188-54e6-269cbc93b3d2"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->-278193295,ExpressionUUID->"6e1c99a5-dcef-9c28-1623-100ed49be772"],

Cell["Construct the Hamiltonian and evolve the state exactly:", "CodeText",
 CellID->-351715035,ExpressionUUID->"608e87cc-8fce-afdf-10b5-1e962a78f525"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"hHeisenberg", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"J", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
     RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", " ", "/@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<XX\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<YY\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<ZZ\>\""}],
        "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"psiT", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
   RowBox[{"hHeisenberg", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<01\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", "t"}], 
   "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[14]:= ",
 CellID->1142857947,ExpressionUUID->"2aa912c6-4938-1bb7-5a56-8ba068cd699d"],

Cell["\<\
Trace out the second spin and ask for the von Neumann entropy:\
\>", "CodeText",
 CellID->-1292164210,ExpressionUUID->"66b4bee0-d247-b105-0e4b-37cde7f3006f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"entropy", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"QuantumPartialTrace", "[", 
      RowBox[{"psiT", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}]}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<VonNeumannEntropy\>\"", 
     "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"t", " ", "J"}], " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[15]:= ",
 CellID->-914169322,ExpressionUUID->"337c2d89-644e-5b5e-6103-c4d30dfb29a4"],

Cell["\<\
The answer is the binary entropy of the two exchange populations. It is zero \
at product states and reaches one bit at the Bell points.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->-1173232819,ExpressionUUID->"5f7c2741-1c81-ec9b-0503-bf2b9535b6e1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Plot the complete entanglement history for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["J", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "644cc522-c7c4-9b18-0c73-dc8ff276e662"],
 ":"
}], "CodeText",
 CellID->-96071603,ExpressionUUID->"2de8c8f9-eaf3-8e90-5b97-e1a28e87d4fa"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"entropy", " ", "/.", " ", 
    RowBox[{"J", " ", "->", " ", "1"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "Pi"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<entanglement entropy [bits]\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
   "    ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[16]:= ",
 CellID->-674748656,ExpressionUUID->"6801f052-da94-0b6f-183e-ea1fdf2159b5"],

Cell["\<\
The state, its reduced density matrix, and a nonlinear entanglement measure \
have all remained exact functions of time.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->801168371,ExpressionUUID->"0daf8e98-7628-e40b-3b54-27c203c2cf51"],

Cell["Noise and measurement use the same object model", "Section",
 CellID->2099374555,ExpressionUUID->"7b6211f5-475c-1194-2911-88bf72e963fe"],

Cell["\<\
Closed evolution is only one part of quantum mechanics. A channel is a \
first-class object, so a symbolic state can pass directly through a \
nonunitary process.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->-2081464990,ExpressionUUID->"7c8f7bdf-2493-8d8a-24b5-72994d27d7d0"],

Cell["Construct a generic Bloch-sphere state:", "CodeText",
 CellID->950596765,ExpressionUUID->"14e8dcaf-74c9-37ba-3c97-d5097d7d9d80"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"qubit", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "/", "2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{"I", " ", "\[Phi]"}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "/", "2"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[17]:= ",
 CellID->1721802074,ExpressionUUID->"5d5cbd3a-e88d-ee42-0b63-35678939b4a8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compute the purity lost under amplitude damping with probability ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b7fe4cc-5889-7f4e-6904-fd96593c4594"],
 ":"
}], "CodeText",
 CellID->-295294457,ExpressionUUID->"6cb5c01f-62f5-68e0-144a-da5916803aca"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"purityLoss", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"qubit", "[", "\"\<Purity\>\"", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"QuantumChannel", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<AmplitudeDamping\>\"", "[", "\[Gamma]", "]"}], "]"}], "[",
        "qubit", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Purity\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[Phi]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"0", " ", "<=", " ", "\[Gamma]", " ", "<=", " ", "1"}]}], 
     "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[18]:= ",
 CellID->86760064,ExpressionUUID->"55f417ec-7166-d78d-038b-8eb60010bdd7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The exact result is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "-", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "4"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "/", "2"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b6e5dad-9702-0c1f-7916-54f722b75765"],
 ". It immediately reveals what numerical cases obscure: the azimuth is \
irrelevant, the ground state is fixed, and full relaxation is pure again."
}], "Text",
 CellID->-533411832,ExpressionUUID->"1d359769-845f-cd94-44ca-0f332deb97fe"],

Cell["\<\
Generalized measurements fit the same algebra. A tetrahedral SIC POVM has \
four outcomes and is informationally complete for a qubit.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->811289931,ExpressionUUID->"2055bfee-d4b5-7aa2-506a-36cbdd404888"],

Cell["\<\
Construct the measurement and apply the Born rule symbolically to all four \
effects:\
\>", "CodeText",
 CellID->-1795218538,ExpressionUUID->"64c30c0d-1857-1b13-0cf0-a65799e26679"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"sic", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "QuantumMeasurementOperator", "[", "\"\<TetrahedronSICPOVM\>\"", "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"probabilities", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{"ComplexExpand", "[", "\n", "    ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"qubit", "[", "\"\<DensityMatrix\>\"", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Normal", "[", "#", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{"sic", "[", "\"\<POVMElements\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}], 
   "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[19]:= ",
 CellID->-2053941492,ExpressionUUID->"46632a09-cc5f-b0ef-6e10-cc52e5eb0235"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Verify normalization for every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ea251ed-865f-e03c-1652-48b733ebb306"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a0bfbe-b1d4-2428-535f-36fbc0668f72"],
 " at once:"
}], "CodeText",
 CellID->-1504392426,ExpressionUUID->"04786d0e-016a-d127-2c07-8568b01ca00d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Total", "[", "probabilities", "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\[Theta]", ",", " ", "\[Phi]"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "Reals"}], 
    "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[20]:= ",
 CellID->-1776389786,ExpressionUUID->"2d15b43a-cd49-5244-5b2a-2e67e4fc20ae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The result is ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d1ff276-b82a-c3ca-5b24-f43039dc9110"],
 ". States, channels, and measurements do not require separate workflows. \
They compose and expose the same property-based interface."
}], "Text",
 CellID->-496883623,ExpressionUUID->"14fd1512-f616-8834-3c82-8d5f83a0db1e"],

Cell["Change the basis, keep the physics", "Section",
 CellID->-1302480555,ExpressionUUID->"66c67103-72a1-9427-0efe-696d0755ff0d"],

Cell["\<\
A useful basis can turn a difficult description into a transparent one. The \
framework stores the basis with each object and reconciles different bases \
during composition.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1748610619,ExpressionUUID->"48c794f4-84f6-2bfc-78fc-0dbe2c8379c6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Define a spin-1 particle in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "=", "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58ee7ecb-1370-1005-0896-7795a605636f"],
 " eigenstate:"
}], "CodeText",
 CellID->-1689710315,ExpressionUUID->"11d04a92-cbef-a8a5-47e0-63dfed9bfa8f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"mx", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<JX\>\"", "[", "1", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[21]:= ",
 CellID->1977961370,ExpressionUUID->"7d9821c9-0e61-bc6d-2ba7-b893ab1506b7"],

Cell["\<\
Rewrite the same state in the three-dimensional computational basis:\
\>", "CodeText",
 CellID->1183845132,ExpressionUUID->"3181a460-bc62-f1ee-67be-3e4a3514c334"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"mxZ", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
    RowBox[{"mx", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Computational\>\"", "[", "3", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"mx", ",", " ", "mxZ"}], "}"}], " ", "//", " ", 
  "TraditionalForm"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[22]:= ",
 CellID->913947769,ExpressionUUID->"3937e1d4-04c3-e55a-68cc-f89ead77cfa0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One representation is a single ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["J", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b45e796-37a7-eecc-197a-fed04253b416"],
 " eigenket. The other is a three-term superposition. Test the invariant in \
both representations:"
}], "CodeText",
 CellID->-224896370,ExpressionUUID->"5e187950-8ca2-2ab2-0638-711a25577898"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"jx", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<JX\>\"", "[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"mx", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
     RowBox[{"jx", "[", "mx", "]"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<Scalar\>\"", "]"}], ",",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"mxZ", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
     RowBox[{"jx", "[", "mxZ", "]"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<Scalar\>\"", "]"}]}], 
  "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[23]:= ",
 CellID->1049687754,ExpressionUUID->"250a2d7c-9b81-05b0-5309-c5261e346f9a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both expectations are ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15a9104d-5625-6af3-4356-8a1763d038d9"],
 ". The coordinates changed; the state and its measurable content did not."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1150298084,ExpressionUUID->"58c17d8b-1b7e-6f79-08ff-74d59e0b3243"],

Cell["The same algebra reaches Fock space", "Section",
 CellID->1528521715,ExpressionUUID->"43821c38-6720-b4f9-71b1-966212da1ec3"],

Cell["\<\
Qubits are not the boundary. The continuous-variable extension supplies \
bosonic operators and states in a truncated Fock basis.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->-876800782,ExpressionUUID->"341c54d9-3079-6bba-5c24-4d83410c3980"],

Cell["\<\
Construct the annihilation operator and a symbolic coherent state:\
\>", "CodeText",
 CellID->1067291743,ExpressionUUID->"1dbf9c2b-d84a-d79b-4b44-1674d9fcbde1"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"a", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AnnihilationOperator", "[", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"alphaKet", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"CoherentState", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Normalized\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "False"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[24]:= ",
 CellID->1392313809,ExpressionUUID->"0f449897-1a0e-51e7-357b-11d19fbb23cd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Check the defining equation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d5a63ab-93b9-14f3-1b7a-7af5264c7ed9"],
 " away from the truncation edge:"
}], "CodeText",
 CellID->349818863,ExpressionUUID->"5077c06e-c394-b43c-000c-da4bf6261f06"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Most", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"a", "[", "alphaKet", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[FormalAlpha]", " ", "alphaKet"}]}], ")"}], 
    "[", "\"\<AmplitudesList\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[25]:= ",
 CellID->-1744382990,ExpressionUUID->"07359582-e823-44a1-2eca-0cef89d62e8b"],

Cell["\<\
Every returned amplitude is zero. The code is finite-dimensional, but the \
symbolic identity survives throughout the represented sector.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1178168612,ExpressionUUID->"7c239bd0-3ff5-3b18-25d0-129ab9818662"],

Cell["\<\
Photon correlations then distinguish three physically different states of \
light:\
\>", "CodeText",
 CellID->-105424996,ExpressionUUID->"68c76573-72ce-0c1a-18fd-7d3d077b5760"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"g2", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"<|", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\"\<Fock\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"G2Coherence", "[", 
      RowBox[{"FockState", "[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Coherent\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"G2Coherence", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"CoherentState", "[", "20", "]"}], "[", "1.5", "]"}], "]"}]}], 
    ",", "\n", "    ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Thermal\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"G2Coherence", "[", 
      RowBox[{"ThermalState", "[", 
       RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", "20"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "|>"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[26]:= ",
 CellID->113307261,ExpressionUUID->"6184d2f2-049e-728e-17bb-cbbcad2b40d4"],

Cell["\<\
Display antibunched, coherent, and bunched statistics together:\
\>", "CodeText",
 CellID->-62456908,ExpressionUUID->"4fd967ef-5008-0b29-75e7-7ec961bd5673"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"BarChart", "[", 
  RowBox[{"g2", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ChartLabels", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", "\"\<g2(0)\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "2.2"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[27]:= ",
 CellID->1313159114,ExpressionUUID->"19bb1c5e-57ab-6e36-4f58-9618625e351c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The values are ",
 Cell[BoxData["0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c8dcc56-7aa9-964a-04b2-e6107f5dfc90"],
 ", numerically ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30baa1c8-66ad-75e0-6059-389213585fca"],
 ", and approximately ",
 Cell[BoxData["2"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52535901-cb26-8b9c-0261-516aeed0d9e6"],
 ". The tiny deviations from the ideal coherent and thermal values are the \
visible cost of Fock-space truncation, not statistical noise."
}], "Text",
 CellID->-970710207,ExpressionUUID->"323a4b1c-b138-a791-63da-6359c0b20dfb"],

Cell["\<\
A cat state makes the phase-space distinction more vivid. Its Wigner function \
can be negative, while its Gaussian-smoothed Husimi function cannot.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->-720885545,ExpressionUUID->"7421cf44-a1ac-4319-1dde-e721d0592e63"],

Cell["\<\
Compute both representations of the same cat state before the live session:\
\>", "CodeText",
 CellID->2114284649,ExpressionUUID->"511b3347-8d7d-ab60-0738-ab212409f64a"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"cat", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"CatState", "[", "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"wigner", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"WignerRepresentation", "[", 
    RowBox[{"cat", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "6"}], ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "2"}], ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<GridSize\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "90"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"husimi", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"HusimiQRepresentation", "[", 
    RowBox[{"cat", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "6"}], ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "3"}], ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<GridSize\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "90"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[28]:= ",
 CellID->1902527339,ExpressionUUID->"36c19c85-764d-0b01-5efe-15ef03f8566b"],

Cell["Show the two phase-space surfaces side by side:", "CodeText",
 CellID->-1266045906,ExpressionUUID->"6815cd54-0cd7-196f-182a-e51ea5626bb5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Plot3D", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"wigner", "[", 
       RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "p"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"-", "6"}], ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"p", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"-", "2"}], ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Mesh", " ", "->", " ", "None"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ColorFunction", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<SunsetColors\>\""}], ",", 
      " ", 
      RowBox[{"PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Wigner\>\""}]}], "]"}], ",", 
    "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"Plot3D", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"husimi", "[", 
       RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "p"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"-", "6"}], ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"p", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"-", "3"}], ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Mesh", " ", "->", " ", "None"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ColorFunction", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<SunsetColors\>\""}], ",", 
      " ", 
      RowBox[{"PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Husimi\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], 
   "}"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[29]:= ",
 CellID->-240081248,ExpressionUUID->"519775d4-d545-25f2-07ad-6c91dcf18fd8"],

Cell["\<\
The Wigner interference fringes dip below zero. The Husimi surface retains \
the two coherent lobes but smooths those fringes away. Both pictures came \
from the same state object.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1703408161,ExpressionUUID->"5900aac7-5263-773e-0f3f-43a167165a04"],

Cell["A symbolic circuit can change its representation", "Section",
 CellID->-626152095,ExpressionUUID->"06ecfdb3-2197-c9b0-2e93-f4fd50239b9a"],

Cell["\<\
A circuit remains symbolic underneath its diagram. This makes exact circuit \
identities available to the ordinary algebra of Wolfram Language.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->849154310,ExpressionUUID->"12d95fcb-3316-2212-42e7-569546a37178"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compose two opposite rotations without assigning a value to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "733995c2-f5bf-78ee-22c6-0caffc4a4a34"],
 ":"
}], "CodeText",
 CellID->-253716686,ExpressionUUID->"4f8ab258-7e7f-0723-7589-34027b0a6a09"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"cancellation", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<RZ\>\"", "[", "\[Phi]", "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<RZ\>\"", "[", 
       RowBox[{"-", "\[Phi]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Parameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "\[Phi]", "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[30]:= ",
 CellID->2037273134,ExpressionUUID->"6b12ee74-9953-131d-1921-003e18e67e67"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Convert the circuit to its operator and simplify under the physical \
assumption that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "65262d3c-fccc-1dc6-0cdd-c579f579672c"],
 " is real:"
}], "CodeText",
 CellID->157021156,ExpressionUUID->"5e157ee2-48da-d240-062b-77cc696ca0aa"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "cancellation", "]"}], 
     "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Phi]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[31]:= ",
 CellID->-494173576,ExpressionUUID->"78287f93-0f12-7c52-2828-76ddaaa746b8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The result is the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Times]", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "08285353-0e0e-39f8-3828-4b1dabb88bc2"],
 " identity matrix. This is semantic simplification: the equality is proved \
for the whole parameter family, not inferred from selected angles or from the \
appearance of a diagram."
}], "Text",
 CellID->-851805568,ExpressionUUID->"1daed7d3-93e8-7698-4b55-ce9d259d5ce2"],

Cell["\<\
The abstraction also separates a circuit from the engine that evaluates it. \
The default circuit path is a tensor-network contraction, and the network is \
inspectable.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->-1742648442,ExpressionUUID->"187adc3d-3961-76c2-4819-d667b8145c28"],

Cell["Expose the tensor network behind the QAOA circuit:", "CodeText",
 CellID->-967789526,ExpressionUUID->"641c78eb-7f03-7846-0c24-71b57ab64aac"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"oneLayer", "[", "\"\<TensorNetworkGraph\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[32]:= ",
 CellID->-1159771408,ExpressionUUID->"5bfcc75d-c21d-6fb0-0983-df06f7a8359a"],

Cell["\<\
The gate diagram describes the algorithm. This graph describes the \
contraction problem that computes it.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->-1258051102,ExpressionUUID->"112ae6ec-4b5c-6ad2-4729-ffb66ee93838"],

Cell["\<\
For Clifford circuits, the same object can instead compile to an exact \
stabilizer tableau. A three-qubit cluster state is a compact check.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->-1870737327,ExpressionUUID->"6121b9de-dddd-aca8-10de-309bd469f6f2"],

Cell["Build the cluster circuit:", "CodeText",
 CellID->1677833016,ExpressionUUID->"30209679-023a-ee91-61df-0823b7ccb4fb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"cluster", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<H\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Range", "[", "3", "]"}]}], ",", " ", "\"\<CZ\>\"", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<CZ\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[33]:= ",
 CellID->25808132,ExpressionUUID->"29bc1606-c22d-409d-5f43-8863f7d812e7"],

Cell["\<\
Evaluate it through two representations and compare the resulting state \
vectors:\
\>", "CodeText",
 CellID->1542447368,ExpressionUUID->"7bf1e1bf-5b3e-c64b-298e-f8f95ec8ac91"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"stabilizer", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"cluster", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Stabilizer\>\""}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "stabilizer", "]"}], 
   "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", "]"}], " ", "===", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"cluster", "[", "]"}], "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", 
   "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[34]:= ",
 CellID->721584768,ExpressionUUID->"3119d855-3ffd-7401-6726-d21fb9885f6b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The result is ",
 Cell[BoxData["True"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62a6d1b5-4e36-fa69-125d-c8ff6bc0c8b3"],
 ". The physical object stays fixed while the computational representation \
changes."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2142431931,ExpressionUUID->"7c41cdc9-5ab3-1ef5-247e-e4935f4664df"],

Cell["What the framework changes", "Section",
 CellID->-1801303399,ExpressionUUID->"51fce014-dca1-0630-0783-fa51d5546d1a"],

Cell["\<\
The unifying idea is now concrete. A symbolic parameter can begin in a state \
or circuit and end in a Bloch vector, optimization landscape, entropy, purity \
loss, or measurement distribution. The same objects survive changes of basis, \
changes of physical model, and changes of computational engine.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->-31957173,ExpressionUUID->"657c1c65-980e-511d-1303-964f19bb2067"],

Cell["\<\
This matters because the final expression is often the scientific result. A \
formula can be differentiated, optimized, simplified, checked in limiting \
cases, and reused as input to the rest of Wolfram Language. The workflow \
remains compact because the objects retain the structure of the physics.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->933913385,ExpressionUUID->"0f15dbd5-5f35-596c-352a-d29f5ac02bb6"],

Cell["What this talk does not show", "Section",
 CellID->-1203482886,ExpressionUUID->"7e9b7e66-629a-1114-26b9-7040172f607e"],

Cell["\<\
This tour omits several substantial parts of the framework: symbolic Lindblad \
master equations, measurement records and feedforward, state tomography, \
explicit contraction-path control, large stabilizer calculations, OpenQASM \
interchange, device transpilation, and hardware execution. Those belong in \
focused follow-up sessions.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->-1420292248,ExpressionUUID->"585a51e6-774f-2dd2-087a-48c002fa7738"],

Cell["\<\
The live emphasis should remain on the seven transitions shown here. They \
make one claim repeatedly, in different physics: the framework is broad \
because its algebra is coherent, not because its function list is long.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->-640064114,ExpressionUUID->"1d7c0b5b-c40c-ea6a-4b03-a304edbeb8b0"],

Cell["References", "Section",
 CellID->393723594,ExpressionUUID->"370294fd-9e49-2d35-5d31-0da71bfc741f"],

